  "description": "rear right\rT1\tLondon Plane x 1\t(Platanus x hispanica) This extra-large plane tree is growing partly over a glass office ceiling. It has been cut back previously, but now requires a harder reduction back towards the edge of the glass. There are cavities on the limb over the roof which shows signs of adaptive growth Suggested work:- Reduce the growth over the glass ceiling back 3-4m to reduce weight. This includes \rremoving some branches roughly 100mm thick. These will be lowered using advanced \rrigging techniques.- Inspect the upper canopy for massaria, remove where necessary. Reduce remaining crown back to previous reduction points  with lots of furnishing growth/ thin remaining points\rrear left\rT2\tTurkey Oak x 1\t(Quercus cerris)\tThis large Turkish oak is being suppressed by the neighbouring plane tree, as such the \tvast majority of the growth is over the courtyard. Suggested work Weight reduce the tips by reducing the lateral growth by 1.5-2m. Remove epicormic growth",
